  "levels_won_this_session": [],
  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 8 has a viable two-stage routing mechanic that prior probes missed: rectangles can be flattened to 22x4, carried through the seven-row horizontal corridor between the upper swatches and the palette wall, recompressed to 4x22 at the upper-right fixture, and then passed without repainting through the true six-cell background opening at x=44..49. The lower fixture restores 4x22 to 7x19 or onward to 16x10. This route preserved color 11 across the wall and placed the 7x19 rectangle exactly over all four color-11 sockets; the second rectangle was independently resized to 16x10 and painted color 6, but budget ended before its analogous wall crossing.",
  "narrative": "Replayed the resolver-provided 519-action prefix from a fresh env.reset() and confirmed frame.levels_completed=7 before exploration. Frame-only exploration found and executed a repaint-safe route for the color-11 rectangle: flatten to 22x4, paint at the upper-left swatch, traverse laterally at y=15..18, compress to 4x22, cross the x=44..49 palette opening, restore to 7x19 at the lower fixture, and place at x=9..15,y=39..57. The second rectangle was resized to the target 16x10 geometry and its color-6 paint leg was confirmed at x=6..21,y=18..27. I stopped at 788 calls because the remaining 12 could not complete its required flatten/corridor/compress crossing; no level-8 win was observed.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The independently verified level-7 prefix is the first 519 actions of this trajectory; this session replayed it once and directly observed levels_completed=7.",
    "The safe palette-wall opening is the six background columns x=44..49. The narrow gaps between framed palette boxes are not safe, even for a 4-wide outline, because paint collision extends beyond the visually empty cells.",
    "A 22x4 outline can move horizontally at y=15..18 without touching either the upper swatches or the palette wall. At y=12..15, adjacency to the color-9 swatch can repaint it despite no obvious fill-cell overlap.",
    "For the color-11 piece, use a wide bbox no farther right than x=3..24 before descending from its paint swatch into the y=15..18 corridor; x=6..27 is close enough to the color-9 swatch to be repainted during the descent.",
    "The successful color-11 placement is a 7x19 outline at x=9..15,y=39..57. The color-6 target geometry is 16x10 at x=6..21,y=45..54.",
    "Normal translation clamps pieces at screen edges; deformation can extend an outline offscreen, so infer the hidden bbox from its cursor and preserved perimeter rather than visible components alone.",
    "Rendered frame buffers mutate in place; copy grids before comparing action deltas."
  ],
  "solve_provenance": "live_agent_self_discovery"
}
